WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.520
Working with the people at Jazz Fest, the people that I work with.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.860
They’re a wonderfully wretched family.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:18.360
Usually, I might see a few of them throughout the year, but when I get together, at the festival, they’re just a wonderful group of people.

4
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.260
A buddy of mine who works there, Mark Courbet.

5
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:28.140
You know, he calls me up at the beginning of the year and he asks, “Are you doing community service this year?”

6
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.740
“Yep.”

7
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.100
And basically what he’s referring to is we don’t get paid that much to work Jazz Fest.

8
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.380
I lose money, everyone loses money to work Jazz Fest.

9
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.180
So why do you do it?

10
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.380
Because of people like Mark, and J.T., Popcorn.

11
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.940
They’re all my wretched family.

12
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.200
In 2003, I almost died.

13
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.900
I got real sick.

14
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.460
I came down with Guillain-Barré syndrome.

15
00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:04.240
The bar I hang out at, they put on a benefit, and the people from Jazz Fest found out about it.

16
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.360
All those people got together and they raised well over six thousand dollars.

17
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:18.340
And that money enabled me to not have to go back to work immediately, and pay my bills, so on and so forth.

18
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.020
So, they took care of me, I’ve got to take care of them.
